<!doctype html>
<html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>{{ meta.study }} — Clinician Report</title>
<style>
 body{font:15px/1.5 -apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:900px;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;color:#1a1a1a}
 h1{font-size:1.5rem;margin-bottom:.2rem} h2{font-size:1.15rem;border-bottom:2px solid #eee;padding-bottom:.2rem;margin-top:1.6rem}
 .sub{color:#666;margin-top:0} table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:.6rem 0;font-size:14px}
 th,td{border:1px solid #ddd;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top} th{background:#f6f8fa}
 .A{border-left:5px solid #c0392b} .B{border-left:5px solid #e67e22} .C{border-left:5px solid #999}
 .pill{display:inline-block;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:10px;font-size:12px;color:#fff}
 .pA{background:#c0392b}.pB{background:#e67e22}.pC{background:#777}
 .note{background:#fff8e1;border:1px solid #ffe082;padding:.7rem 1rem;border-radius:6px}
 .caveat{background:#fdecea;border:1px solid #f5c6cb;padding:.7rem 1rem;border-radius:6px}
 code{background:#f2f2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px}
</style></head><body>
<h1>{{ meta.study }} — Clinical Genetics Report</h1>
<p class="sub">Hyper-IgE syndrome (HIES) exome investigation · generated {{ meta.date }} · familyforge v{{ version }}</p>

<div class="note"><b>Summary.</b>
{% if tierA %}{{ tierA|length }} high-priority (Tier A) candidate finding(s) identified.
The leading candidate is <b>{{ tierA[0].gene }}</b> ({{ tierA[0].zygosity }}, {{ tierA[0].model|replace('_',' ') }}).
{% elif tierB %}No Tier A finding; {{ tierB|length }} Tier B candidate(s) of uncertain significance require review.
{% else %}No high-confidence candidate in the HIES panel met reporting criteria; see caveats and consider re-phenotyping / extended analysis.
{% endif %}
</div>

<h2>Family analysed</h2>
<table><tr><th>Individual</th><th>Role</th><th>Sex</th><th>Sequenced</th></tr>
{% for m in family %}<tr><td>{{ m.iid }}</td><td>{{ m.role }}</td><td>{{ m.sex }}</td><td>{{ 'yes' if m.sequenced else 'no (relationship only)' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
{% if mz_groups %}<p><b>Monozygotic twins:</b> {{ mz_groups|map('join',' + ')|join('; ') }} — treated as genetic replicates (a candidate must be concordant in both).</p>{% endif %}

<h2>Priority findings</h2>
{% if tierA or tierB %}
{% for r in (tierA + tierB) %}
<table class="{{ r.tier }}"><tr><th style="width:22%">Gene / tier</th>
 <td><b>{{ r.gene }}</b> &nbsp;<span class="pill p{{ r.tier }}">Tier {{ r.tier }}</span> · confidence: {{ r.confidence }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Variant</th><td><code>{{ r.locus }}</code> {% if r.rsid and r.rsid != '.' %}({{ r.rsid }}){% endif %}<br>
 {{ r.consequence }} · {{ r.hgvsp if r.hgvsp!='.' else r.hgvsc }}</td></tr>
{% if r.partner %}<tr><th>Second allele</th><td><code>{{ r.partner }}</code></td></tr>{% endif %}
<tr><th>Zygosity / model</th><td>{{ r.zygosity }} · {{ r.model|replace('_',' ') }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Segregation</th><td>{{ r.segregation }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Evidence</th><td>ClinVar: {{ r.clinvar }} · gnomAD: {{ r.gnomad }}{% if r.gnomad_afr and r.gnomad_afr != '.' %} (AFR {{ r.gnomad_afr }}){% endif %} · SIFT: {{ r.sift }} · PolyPhen: {{ r.polyphen }}
{% if r.alphamissense and r.alphamissense != '.' %}<br><b>AlphaMissense: {{ r.alphamissense }}</b> · REVEL: {{ r.revel }} · CADD: {{ r.cadd }}{% endif %}
<br>{{ r.tier_reason }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Interpretation</th><td>{{ r.inheritance_note }}</td></tr>
</table>
{% endfor %}
{% else %}<p>No Tier A/B candidate met criteria. Tier C variants (if any) are listed in the publication report.</p>{% endif %}

<h2>Clinical implications & suggested next steps</h2>
<ul>
{% if top and top.gene == 'DOCK8' %}<li><b>DOCK8 deficiency</b> carries a severe infection/malignancy course — evaluate for <b>haematopoietic stem-cell transplant (HSCT)</b>, and confirm any deletion by MLPA/aCGH.</li>{% endif %}
{% if top and top.gene == 'STAT3' %}<li><b>STAT3 (AD-HIES / Job syndrome)</b> — prophylactic anti-staphylococcal + antifungal management; monitor lung/connective-tissue features.</li>{% endif %}
<li>Confirm any reported variant by orthogonal method (Sanger for SNV/indel; MLPA/aCGH for CNV) before clinical action.</li>
<li>Consider obtaining paternal DNA to confirm inheritance / phase (father not sequenced here).</li>
<li>Correlate with immunology: serum IgE, eosinophils, infection spectrum (bacterial vs viral), dental/skeletal signs, platelet count.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Sample QC</h2>
<table><tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th></tr>
{% for k,v in qc.sex.items() %}<tr><td>Sex — {{ k }}</td><td>declared {{ v.declared_sex }}, inferred {{ v.inferred_sex }} (chrX het {{ v.x_het_rate }})</td></tr>{% endfor %}
{% for k,v in qc.pairwise.items() %}<tr><td>Relatedness — {{ k }}</td><td>genotype concordance {{ v.concordance }} over {{ v.n_sites }} sites</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>

<div class="caveat"><b>Caveats.</b> Father not sequenced — some inheritance/phase calls are inferred and unconfirmed.
gnomAD allele frequencies are from the VEP cache; genome-wide gnomAD/dbNSFP were unavailable, so
common-variant filtering and some in-silico scores are limited. Tier A/B variants are candidates
pending orthogonal confirmation and ACMG classification by a clinical laboratory. This report is a
research analysis, not a diagnostic result.</div>
</body></html>
